# CLAUDE.md

Guidance for Claude Code when working **on this repository**.

> This file is instructions for modifying Claude-Pipeline. It is not the product README.
> For what the project claims to do, see README.md — but read "Known State" below first,
> because README currently describes features that are not implemented.

---

## Known State (read before changing anything)

**The pipeline does not currently execute.** Do not assume any phase has ever run. Verified:

- `.claude/history.json` → `"runs": []`, `"totalRuns": 0`. Zero recorded runs.
- `.claude/artifacts/` does not exist, though four docs reference it as if it ships.
- Every phase invocation passes `--max-tokens`, which is **not a Claude Code CLI flag**.
  Verify: `claude -p --model haiku --max-tokens 100 "hi"` → `error: unknown option '--max-tokens'`.
  17 call sites in `.claude/commands/auto-pipeline.md` (:1052, :1157, :1241, :1328, :1373,
  :1418, :1498, :1527, :1603, :1684, :1710, :1802, :1896, :1938, :1978, :2011, :2157).
- 11 of 13 phase calls read `echo "\$PROMPT"` — an escaped `$`, which pipes the literal
  7-character string `$PROMPT`. The two revision blocks (:1527, :1710) and the canonical
  template (:744) use the correct unescaped form, so the file contradicts itself.
- Helper functions are defined in one ```bash fence and called from another 300–1700 lines
  away (`init_cache_tracking` called :65, defined :405). The Bash tool spawns a fresh shell
  per call — **shell state does not persist between fences.** Nothing in this file is
  executable as written.

**Treat `auto-pipeline.md` as a specification the orchestrating model interprets as prose,
not as a shell script.** Its determinism claims are aspirational.

When you fix something here, fix the doc in the same change. The single largest defect class
in this repo is documentation asserting features that were never implemented.

