## Working On This Repo

### Reading `auto-pipeline.md`
2,418 lines. **Page it with `offset`/`limit`** — never read it once and assume you have it.
Its sections contradict each other (model routing is defined twice at :34 and :691; the
subprocess template at :744 disagrees with all 11 phases that copy it).

### Two orchestrators exist and they diverge
| File | Lines | Model routing | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.claude/commands/auto-pipeline.md` | 2,418 | Yes (`--model`) | The one docs describe |
| `run-pipeline.sh` | 1,038 | **None** — `grep -c 'MODEL\|--model\|haiku\|sonnet' run-pipeline.sh` → 0 | Referenced by zero docs |

`run-pipeline.sh:223` is `echo "$prompt" | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions` with no
`--model`. Every cost claim in every doc is false for this orchestrator. A change to one does
not propagate to the other. **State which orchestrator you are changing.**

### Do not edit `.claude/.claude/`
An install bug (`install.sh:121` `cp -r "$source_dir" "$target_dir"` nests when the target
exists) created a fossil tree: 10 command files including a stale 868-line `auto-pipeline.md`
describing a **different 20-phase pipeline**. Claude Code does not discover it — it is a
sibling of `.claude/commands/`, not a child. Anything you edit there has no effect.

### Verify claims before repeating them
Every count in this file was checked with `ls | wc -l` on 2026-07-15. If you change a count,
re-run the command. Do not copy a number from README — README is wrong about several.

