## Documented-But-Unimplemented Surface

Do not treat these as existing. README:119-134 advertises 13 flags; **one** (`--resume`) is
implemented:

`--dry-run` `--fast` `--fix` `--auto` `--yolo` `--quiet` `--only=X` `--preview` `--test`
`--branch` `--pr` `--template=X` `--estimate` → all zero hits in `auto-pipeline.md`.

Inversely, the flags that **do** work are documented nowhere in README or this file:
`--skip-arm` `--skip-ar` `--skip-pmatch` `--batch-qa` `--mode=dev`.

README's Quick Start (:101) says `/auto-pipeline --yolo "..."`. `--yolo` is not parsed, so it
survives into `$TASK` and is sent to the model as part of the task string. demo/README.md:64
uses the correct `--profile=yolo`. Two docs, opposite syntax, and the wrong one is more
prominent.

Also missing but linked: `LICENSE` (README:5 badge and :523), `CONTRIBUTING.md` (README:515),
`.github/assets/demo.gif` (README:26). A repo whose headline badge claims MIT ships no license
text. `.claude/prompts/` holds 14 externalized phase prompts that `load_prompt()` (:333) never
loads — grep returns exactly one hit, the definition.

